iotroski":33.3,"_gate_spread":-0.21234734139690567,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.08460018946796816,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.18960427851859712,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.021261203574126863,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":35.6,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.07669462434711685,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.037710110732276994,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":53.0,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.017654260569240326,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":70.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.50781,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.943,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":94.3,"pf":[],"description_full":"OPKO Health, Inc. operates as a healthcare company, in the United States, Ireland, Chile, Spain, Israel, Mexico, and internationally. The company operates in two segments, Pharmaceutical and Diagnostics. The Pharmaceutical segment develops MDX2001, a tetra-specific antibody targeting several types of solid tumors in Phase 1 clinical trials; MDX2003, a tetra-specific antibody targeting two antigens for hematological tumors in Phase 1 clinical trials; and MDX2004, a trispecific immune modulator to rebuild and sustain the patient's own immune system. This segment also engages in the development of Epstein Barr Virus vaccine; Rayaldee, a patented extended-release product for oral administration containing 30 mcg of a prohormone; OPK-88006 oral and injectable product to regulate blood glucose and reduce body weight; NGENLA, recombinant human growth hormone product developed for the long-term treatment of pediatric patients with growth hormone deficiency. The Diagnostics segment offers laboratory testing services, such as detection, diagnosis, evaluation, monitoring, and treatment of diseases, as well as esoteric testing, molecular diagnostics, anatomical pathology, genetics, women's health, and correctional healthcare under the BioReference brand; and 4Kscore test. OPKO Health, Inc. was founded in 2006 and is headquartered in Miami, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Phillip  Frost M.D., Ph.D. | Chairman of the Board & CEO | Age 89 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $267K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 25%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Opko Health, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.2B market cap on $607M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -15% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -11% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 36%.","The company is burning through $191M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -1.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 51% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Healthcare peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 19% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 67/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; structural revenue/margin decline \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 196% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Insiders are net buyers (94% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $3.0M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"What Is Drawing Fresh Attention To OPKO Health (OPK)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nasdaq-opk/opko-health/news/what-is-drawing-fresh-attention-to-opko-health-opk","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794617217.251,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.915,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Reviewing OPKO Health (NASDAQ:OPK) and UnitedHealth Group (NYSE:UNH)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/reviewing-opko-health-nasdaqopk-and-unitedhealth-group-nyseunh.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794410117.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.934,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is OPKO Health (OPK) Too Expensive After Its Recent Sales Shift?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nasdaq-opk/opko-health/news/is-opko-health-opk-too-expensive-after-its-recent-sales-shif","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794093510.291,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.607,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Critical Review: OPKO Health (OPK) and Its Rivals","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/critical-review-opko-health-opk-and-its-rivals.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793988920.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.7,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Insider Selling: OPKO Health (NASDAQ:OPK) Director Sells $16,698.50 in Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/insider-selling-opko-health-nasdaqopk-director-sells-16698-50-in-stock.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793917387.0,"origin":"tiingo","senti